      {
        "periodo": "2024",
        "contexto_mercado": "The year 2024 was characterized by strong US economic growth (almost 3%) contrasting with a globally slowing world, particularly China and Germany. This led to disproportionate rises in US stock markets, USD appreciation, and a cautious US Federal Reserve. Rising public debt was a common feature, while inflation continued to fall due to decreasing goods, energy prices, and moderating wage increases. The environment was complex and uncertain, presenting real risks of dislocation.",
        "tesis_gestora": "Given the complex and uncertain environment with risks of dislocation, the manager did not wish to deploy a great deal of risk in markets considered unattractive. The management team aimed to reaffirm the fund's DNA: searching for quality companies with a defensive business model in promising sectors like healthcare, tech/services, IT, and energy transition.",
        "decisiones_tomadas": "The fund adopted a cautious approach, avoiding deploying significant risk. Key strategies included duration management and pure bond strategies. Arbitrage pockets (yield curve, break-even inflation rates) were also utilized. The fund maintained modest exposure to credit. The management focused on investing in quality companies with defensive business models in sectors such as healthcare, tech/services, IT, and energy transition. At year-end, cash (including money market funds) stood at 9.7% of the portfolio.",
        "resultado_real": "The Alpha Bonds sub-fund's performance was slightly behind its indices. All initiated strategy families contributed positively to annual performance, with duration management and pure bond strategies being the biggest contributors. Arbitrage pockets and modest credit exposure had a more limited contribution. The lack of trend and low amplitude in long-term rates reduced bond market volatility, and active duration management did not add significant performance.",
